#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:10
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "Ámbito"

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:12
msgid ""
"The assigned AEAT registry subtree contains 2,140 files totaling "
"96,400,430 bytes: 2,094 TOML files and 46 JSON files. I used the "
"precomputed registry structure index for complete counts and syntax "
"status, then inspected bounded samples from scopes, year policy, "
"authorization enrollment, temporal facts, formulas, model revisions, "
"deadlines and generated layouts. Semantic review is representative and "
"below the 24,000-token cap; in particular, I did not read the large "
"Modelo 200 generated export-provenance files (about 10.8 MB and 10.9 MB "
"each), nor the full multi-megabyte revisions and layout declarations. The"
" index records 2,141 total AEAT/Cadrumo registry files across this chunk "
"and the separate one-file Cadrumo schema chunk, with 2,095 TOML and 46 "
"JSON parsed and no syntax errors. That validates syntax/metadata "
"inventory, not schemas, formulas, tax correctness or legal applicability "
"([registry structure index](../evidence/registry-structure.json))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:14
msgid "Capability and structure"
msgstr "Capacidad y estructura"

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:16
msgid ""
"This is a declarative tax and form registry rather than application code."
" It organizes 58 model directories and 68 named revision directories. "
"Within model revisions the sampled and indexed file families include "
"revision metadata, casillas, formulas, parameters, form/export layouts, "
"filing windows, applicability, cross-references, dependency "
"classifications, and generated exports. The largest model inventories are"
" Modelo 200 (308 files), 303 (124), 390 (99), and 100 (63). Outside the "
"model trees are authorization-scope declarations, facts, legal-source "
"catalogs, IVA territory/catalogue tables, topic indexes, and two records "
"dedicated to the annual Modelo 303 order. The broader layout gives other "
"modules structured fields and source keys to resolve, but no consumer, "
"parser or mutation path is included in this chunk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:18
msgid ""
"The nine apoderamiento scope entries group tax procedures into "
"Spanish/Catalan/English/Hungarian labels and associate selected scopes "
"with model codes. The file documents a versioned “bootstrap” catalogue "
"and describes uppercase codes, repeated `--scope` arguments, and `ALL` as"
" expansion to the union of listed scopes. These are declared interface "
"rules in a data file; the parser and actual AEAT permission semantics are"
" outside this review. A separate `authorization.d` directory has 28 "
"model-specific enrollment records. Samples classify Modelo 100 and 303 as"
" `calculation` evidence and name test-path metadata, but those rows "
"themselves do not grant a real authorization or prove a test ran (scope "
"catalogue (`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/apoderamientos/scopes.toml`),"
" Modelo 100 enrollment "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/authorization.d/100.toml`), Modelo 303 "
"enrollment (`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/authorization.d/303.toml`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:20
msgid "Temporal knowledge and calculations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:22
msgid ""
"Temporal selection is explicit in the sampled registry. `supported-"
"filing-years.toml` sets a floor of 2022 and a horizon of 2026. Its "
"comments define the floor as a hard lower gate, but say the horizon is "
"not a gate and that later years may carry forward the newest eligible "
"authored revision; no `hard_ceiling` is declared. The comments also say "
"unresolved prerequisites are enumerated in an audit that remains advisory"
" until a separate enforcement change. This describes intended policy, but"
" whether the runtime refuses pre-floor years or answers post-horizon "
"years as stated depends on the consumer and must be checked there "
"(supported filing-year policy (`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/legal"
"/supported-filing-years.toml`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:24
msgid ""
"Fact records use typed selectors, legal citations, ownership/review "
"metadata, and effective-date intervals. For example, the IVA rate "
"schedule contains 69 variants and selects on member state, rate kind and "
"rate role along a `devengo_date` axis; historical temporary rates can "
"overlap ordinary tiers and are represented with distinct roles and end "
"dates. A companion recargo fact maps the applied rate to a surcharge and "
"includes legal references. This supports date- and category-sensitive "
"lookup rather than one global constant, but the registry values require "
"legal/source validation outside the static sample (IVA rate schedule "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/facts/0062-iva-rate-schedule.toml`), "
"IVA recargo mapping (`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/facts/0063-iva-"
"recargo-by-applied-rate.toml`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:26
msgid ""
"The sampled Modelo 100 formula declarations show a small expression "
"language: a capital-gain box subtracts one casilla from another and "
"rounds to two decimal places; other declarations use sums and parameter "
"lookups. A regional minimum formula dispatches on the taxpayer's "
"residence community, with source-citation and `required_text` records "
"alongside formulas. This is a meaningful bridge from box definitions and "
"tax parameters to declaration arithmetic, but the declarations do not "
"execute themselves and this inspection does not verify the calculation "
"engine or formula outputs (Modelo 100 formulas and source citations "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/modelos/100/revisions/2025/formulas/0001-declarations.toml`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:28
msgid ""
"Modelo 303's 2026 revision illustrates how these pieces join. It "
"identifies a predecessor and legal/source references, carries filing "
"schedule and live-cross-reference source references from earlier "
"editions, and has 2026 quarterly and monthly deadline windows, including "
"separate payment cutoffs for some monthly periods. The record says "
"weekend/holiday movement occurs at read time. Its generated form-layout "
"TOML records design-source hashes and casilla-to-box placements. The "
"revision's own review note says coverage was measured after binding "
"derivation, that the revision has no fresh-render reproduction evidence, "
"that the numbers are not attested as legally correct, and that its "
"reviewer token is pending operator sign-off. The source also explicitly "
"says the inherited live references and schedule were not re-grounded "
"against this edition's design. Those disclosures are useful controls on "
"claims: they establish an agent-prepared mapping and its stated limits, "
"not a completed human/legal certification (Modelo 303 2026 revision "
"metadata "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/modelos/303/revisions/2026-y-siguientes/revision.toml`),"
" deadline windows "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/modelos/303/revisions/2026-y-siguientes/deadline_windows/0001-declarations.toml`),"
" generated form layout "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/modelos/303/revisions/2026-y-siguientes/form_layouts/0001"
"-form-layout.toml`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:30
msgid ""
"Modelo 721's 2024 revision demonstrates an applicability decision "
"separate from filing-format authority. It selects 2024 onward and records"
" the 2024 BOE amendment as applying “for the first time” to 2024 "
"declarations filed in 2025; the `reviewed_by` note interprets this as a "
"continuing, open-ended applicability window. The same note expressly does"
" not claim a complete AEAT service-package, serializer, validation matrix"
" or filing-grade record design because the historic service description "
"is not pair-complete in the bundle. Its separate deadline file carries "
"annual windows through 2026. This is a reasoned registry decision with "
"candid limits, not independent proof of filing-service compatibility "
"(Modelo 721 applicability revision "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/modelos/721/revisions/2024/revision.toml`),"
" Modelo 721 deadline windows "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/modelos/721/revisions/2024/deadline_windows/0001-declarations.toml`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:32
msgid "Security, quality and follow-up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:34
msgid ""
"The registry contains model field definitions and authorization-scope "
"vocabulary, but no credentials or customer declarations were identified "
"in the samples. A scope catalog is not an access-control implementation: "
"synthesis should verify the command parser, authorization checks, "
"provider credentials and actual AEAT calls before concluding that a "
"listed scope limits user access. Likewise, `review_status = "
"\"agent_reviewed\"` is a provenance label, not an external authority; the"
" sampled files make that distinction explicit in their review notes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:36
msgid ""
"One bounded schema question should be checked in the consuming code: the "
"Modelo 303 enrollment record uses the field name `renta_years = [2025, "
"2026]`, while its model is IVA and its comment describes a cross-Renta "
"compensation-carry calculation. This may be a deliberate generic "
"enrollment key for cross-model calculation cases; the registry alone "
"cannot show whether the loader expects that exact key or whether it "
"changes reachable behavior. Do not treat it as a product defect until the"
" admission path is traced (Modelo 303 enrollment "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/registry/aeat/authorization.d/303.toml`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/203-aeat-registry-and-model-declarations.md:38
msgid ""
"The main strengths are versioned model coverage, declarative formulas and"
" layouts, effective-date selectors, legal/source links, and review notes "
"that state what their evidence does and does not establish. The open "
"questions are runtime resolution of `floor`/`horizon`, legal sign-off and"
" source coverage for recent revisions, whether inherited references stay "
"valid after layout changes, and whether export/form-layout generators "
"match their checked-in artifacts. Static syntax success alone answers "
"none of those questions. No runtime, tests or live AEAT interaction are "
"part of this chunk."
msgstr ""

